.TH BLOCKTOOLS 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
blocktools \- host wrapper that runs a pipeline in the sealed container
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&./blocktools run    '<pipeline>'   # agent\-safe: prints only addresses/paths/statuses
\&./blocktools reveal '<pipeline>'   # human only: needs a TTY + typed code, prints keys
\&./blocktools build
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Thin host\-side wrapper. Runs a blocktools pipeline in a sealed container.
Inputs: $BLOCKTOOLS_IN (default ./in) mounted read\-only at /in.
Secrets (passwords/passphrases) : $BLOCKTOOLS_SECRETS (default ./secrets) read\-only at /secrets.
.SH OPTIONS
See SYNOPSIS; this tool has no separate long\-option list beyond \-\-help.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
Inputs: $BLOCKTOOLS_IN (default ./in) mounted read\-only at /in.
Secrets (passwords/passphrases) : $BLOCKTOOLS_SECRETS (default ./secrets) read\-only at /secrets.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success (JSON lines may still carry status fields such as done / no_candidates).
.TP
2
Bad input, unsupported shape, or tool\-reported failure (JSON status is the detail).
.TP
3
Refused on purpose (watch\-only, policy deny, human abort, missing confirmation).
.PP
Other nonzero codes are tool\-specific; always read the last JSON status line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
See recipes/ for end\-to\-end flows. Search for blocktools in recipes/*.md.
\&./blocktools run 'classify < /in/seed.txt'
\&./blocktools run 'seed\-repair < /in/seed.txt | seed\-to\-master | derive \-\-chain btc \-\-count 1'
\&./blocktools run 'classify /in/algo\-mnemonic.txt'
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: audit before use with real funds. See docs/SECURITY.md.
Run secret\-touching tools only inside ./blocktools run (sealed, offline).
.SH SEE ALSO
blocktools(7), docs/SECURITY.md, docs/getting\-started.md, recipes/README.md
